From 54643f76ce32aa84d92aa672539b6233dccab772 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:21:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 523/526] Model loading: the b12x load format and its in-tree
 adapter go

--load-format direct (0499) is B12X's bounce-mode O_DIRECT loader ported
into vLLM, and the recipe loads with it (VLLM_PLUGINS empty). The in-tree
adapter of B12X's loader (model_loader/b12x_loader.py, the "b12x" load
format) imports B12X's loader package and has no other user:

- b12x_loader.py and its test go; "b12x" leaves LoadFormats and
  get_model_loader no longer registers it lazily.
- The B12X executor-output test's weight-loading panel case goes (the
  panel was the B12X loader's); its preparation-output cases stay.
- direct_loader.py and the streaming-loading design note name the adapter
  as gone.
